ments":[[163,["we read 8 bytes at a time (u64) but only actually consume 6 of those bytes. Thus, we need","2 trailing bytes to be available to read.."]],[169,["Major performance wins from letting the optimizer do the bounds check once, mostly","on the output side"]],[179,["Hand-unrolling for 32 vs 16 or 8 bytes produces yields performance about equivalent","to unsafe pointer code on a Xeon E5-1650v3. 64 byte unrolling was slightly better for","large inputs but significantly worse for 50-byte input, unsurprisingly. I suspect","that it's a not uncommon use case to encode smallish chunks of data (e.g. a 64-byte","SHA-512 digest), so it would be nice if that fit in the unrolled loop at least once.","Plus, single-digit percentage performance differences might well be quite different","on different hardware."]],[230,["Encode what's left after the fast loop."]],[237,["start at the first index not handled by fast loop, which may be 0."]]]}}},{"def_id":19,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["num",0]},{"Impl":{"Ty":{"params":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"Deduplicated":0},"kind":"InherentImplBlock"}}},{"Ident":["saturating_sub",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":17,"beg":{"line":2569,"col":8},"end":{"line":2569,"col":60}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Saturating integer subtraction. Computes `self - rhs`, saturating"},{"DocComment":" at the numeric bounds instead of overflowing."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(100usize.saturating_sub(27), 73);"},{"DocComment":"assert_eq!(13usize.saturating_sub(127), 0);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Always","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null,"has_er